ENTRY            11197   20140206   20140604   20140530       1397
SUBENT        11197001   20140206   20140604   20140530       1397
BIB                  9         23
TITLE      Neutron cross sections of the boron isotopes for
           energies between 10 and 500 keV
AUTHOR     (F.P.Mooring,J.E.Monahan,C.M.Huddleston)
REFERENCE  (J,NP,82,16,1966)
           #doi:10.1016/0029-5582(66)90520-7
INSTITUTE  (1USAANL)
FACILITY   (VDG,1USAANL)
PART-DET   (N)
DETECTOR   (BF3) System consists of 34 BF3 counters suspended
           in mineral oil contained in a cylindrical tank 79 cm
           in diam. This inner tank is surrounded by an annular
           shield tank which has an outside diameter of 137 cm
           and is filled with a saturated solution of NaBO2.
METHOD     (TRN) The measurements reported here consisted of a
           sequence of runs at each neutron energy En. For each
           run, the neutrons counted were those transmitted
           through a transmission sample and scattered by a
           detector sample.
HISTORY    (19760628T) Translated from SCISRS
           (19800814A) converted to reaction formalism
           (20140206A) BP: Digitized Fig. 3, added doi, updated
           all subentries to new date formats, lower case.
           Corrections according last EXFOR rules and Dict.
ENDBIB              23
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           26
